#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:1
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:3
msgid "Gazebo libraries are not found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:4
msgid "If you see this error message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:6
msgid ""
"I cannot find any available 'gz' command:\n"
"\t* Did you install any Gazebo library?\n"
"\t* Did you set the GZ_CONFIG_PATH environment variable?\n"
"\t    E.g.: export GZ_CONFIG_PATH=$HOME/local/share/gz\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:13
msgid "You should set up the environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:15
msgid ""
"# replace <path_to_install_dir> to your Gazebo installation directory\n"
"GZ_CONFIG_PATH=<path_to_install_dir>/share/gz/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:20
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:22
msgid "Maximum number of open files reached `ulimit` error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:23
msgid ""
"When installing using homebrew, you may see the following error message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:25
msgid ""
"Error: The maximum number of open files on this system has been reached. Use "
"'ulimit -n' to increase this limit.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:29
msgid ""
"As suggested in the error message, run the command below and check the "
"output. The default value is set to `256` which is too low."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:30
msgid "ulimit -n\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:34
msgid ""
"Run the following command to increase the open files `ulimit` and then "
"proceed with the homebrew install:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:35
msgid "ulimit -n 10240\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:39
msgid "Unable to find `urdf_model.h` error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:40
msgid ""
"After installing all the dependencies and starting the build process, you "
"may encounter an error that looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:42
msgid ""
"/Users/user/jetty_ws/src/sdformat/src/parser_urdf.cc:30:10: fatal error: "
"'urdf_model/model.h' file not found\n"
"#include <urdf_model/model.h>\n"
"         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"1 error generated.\n"
"make[2]: *** [src/CMakeFiles/sdformat9.dir/parser_urdf.cc.o] Error 1\n"
"make[1]: *** [src/CMakeFiles/sdformat9.dir/all] Error 2\n"
"make: *** [all] Error 2\n"
"Failed   <<< sdformat9\t[ Exited with code 2 ]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:53
msgid ""
"First check if `urdfdom` and `urdfdom_headers` are installed by running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:55
msgid "brew install urdfdom urdfdom_headers\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:59
msgid ""
"Then if the error persists, compile with the internal version of `urdfdom` "
"by running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:61
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DUSE_INTERNAL_URDF=ON --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:65
msgid ""
"This command will ignore the system installation of `urdfdom` and use the "
"internal version instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:67
msgid "Unable to load .dylib file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:68
msgid ""
"When running the `gz sim -s` command, an error like the one below may show "
"up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:70
msgid ""
"Error while loading the library [/Users/jetty/jetty_ws/install/lib//libgz-"
"physics6-dartsim-plugin.6.dylib]: dlopen(/Users/jetty/jetty_ws/install/lib//"
"libgz-physics6-dartsim-plugin.6.dylib, 5): Library not loaded: @rpath/"
"libIrrXML.dylib\n"
"  Referenced from: /usr/local/opt/assimp/lib/libassimp.5.dylib\n"
"  Reason: image not found\n"
"[Err] [Physics.cc:275] Unable to load the /Users/jetty/jetty_ws/install/lib//"
"libgz-physics6-dartsim-plugin.6.dylib library.\n"
"Escalating to SIGKILL on [Gazebo Sim Server]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:78
msgid ""
"The issue is related to OSX System Integrity Protection (SIP). The "
"workaround is to run `gz` with a different ruby then make sure that ruby is "
"loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:80
msgid ""
"brew install ruby\n"
"\n"
"# Add the following to ~/.bashrc\n"
"export PATH=/usr/local/Cellar/ruby/2.6.5/bin:$PATH\n"
"\n"
"# Source ~/.bashrc in terminal\n"
". ~/.bashrc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:90
msgid ""
"No rule to make target `'/usr/lib/libm.dylib', needed by 'lib/libgz-physics6-"
"dartsim-plugin.6.1.0.dylib'. Stop.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:91
msgid ""
"Try to run `brew outdated` followed by a `brew upgrade` may fix some of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:93
msgid "Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:95
msgid "Out of memory issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:97
msgid ""
"There can be out of memory issue during the compilation of Gazebo, "
"especially during compilation of gz-physics. To prevent out of memory issues "
"you can restrict the number of jobs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:100
msgid "MAKEFLAGS=\"-j<Number of jobs> \" colcon build --executor sequential\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:104
msgid "Problems with dual Intel and Nvidia GPU systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:106
msgid ""
"If you are using a dual Intel/Nvidia system it could be the case that the "
"simulator is being run under Intel instead of using the Nvidia GPU. Bugs can "
"vary but there could problems with shadows, incorrect laser scans or other "
"rendering related issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:111
msgid "prime-select command line tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:113
msgid ""
"Hybrid Intel/Nvidia systems can be configured using the command line tool "
"prime-select. One option is to use always Nvidia:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:116
msgid ""
"sudo prime-select nvidia\n"
"# logout user session and login again\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:119
msgid ""
"Other option is to configure the render offload for OpenGL applications to "
"use Nvidia. This means that your X screen and all normal applications are "
"handled by the Intel GPU, but all OpenGL applications that you start from "
"the terminal (including Gazebo) are rendered on the Nvidia GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:124
msgid ""
"# place the lines in your .bashrc if you want the change to be permanent\n"
"export __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1\n"
"export __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia\n"
"# logout user session and login again\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:129
msgid "nvidia-settings GUI tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:131
msgid ""
"nvidia-settings is a GUI program that helps to configure the options for the "
"Nvidia graphic cards and includes some controls for hybrid Intel/Nvidia:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:134
msgid ""
"The section \"PRIME Profiles\" can be used to select that the Nvidia card "
"controls all the GUI applications by selecting \"NVIDIA (Performance Mode)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:137
msgid ""
"The \"Application Profiles\" can control the use of the Nvidia GPU per "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:139
msgid "Unable to create the rendering window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:141
msgid ""
"If you're getting errors like \"Unable to create the rendering window\", it "
"could mean you're using an old OpenGL version. Gazebo Sim uses the Ogre 2 "
"rendering engine by default, which requires an OpenGL version higher than "
"3.3, preferably 4.3+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:146
msgid ""
"This can be confirmed by checking the Ogre 2 logs at `~/.gz/rendering/ogre2."
"log`, which should have an error like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:149
msgid ""
"\"OGRE EXCEPTION(3:RenderingAPIException): OpenGL 3.3 is not supported. "
"Please update your graphics card drivers.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:151
msgid "You can also check your OpenGL version running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:153
msgid "glxinfo | grep \"OpenGL version\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:155
msgid ""
"To enable Ogre 2 support, you'll need to update your computer's OpenGL "
"version. As suggested on the Ogre logs, this may require updating your "
"graphics card drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:159
msgid ""
"If you still run into OpenGL issues when running Gazebo with Ogre 2, it "
"could be that certain extensions are not supported by your driver or you are "
"running inside a virtual machine. In this case, you can try disabling DRI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:163
msgid "export LIBGL_DRI3_DISABLE=1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:165
msgid "or force software rendering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:167
msgid "export LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:169
msgid ""
"If you are using MESA drivers, you can also try overriding the OpenGL version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:171
msgid ""
"# Override GL version to 3.3\n"
"export MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=3.3\n"
"\n"
"# Alternatively, select Core + Forward compatible profile with 3.3\n"
"export MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=3.3FC\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:177
msgid ""
"See the [MESA environment variable documentation](https://docs.mesa3d.org/"
"envvars.html#envvar-MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:180
msgid ""
"The Ogre 2 debs from the osrfoundation repository are built from a fork of "
"Ogre's `v2-3` branch with changes needed for deb packaging and allowing it "
"to be co-installable with Ogre 1.x. The code can be found here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:184
msgid "https://github.com/osrf/ogre-2.3-release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:186
msgid ""
"You should be able to use Ogre 1 without any issues however. You can check "
"if that's working by running with Ogre 1 instead of Ogre 2, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:189
msgid "gz sim -v 3 shapes.sdf --render-engine ogre\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:191
msgid ""
"If that loads, you can continue to use Gazebo with Ogre 1, just use the `--"
"render-engine ogre` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:194
msgid "Wayland issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:196
msgid ""
"There's an issue with the interaction of Ogre and Qt in Gazebo that prevents "
"wayland from working properly. You might see an error message like the one "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:199
msgid ""
"Unable to create the rendering window: OGRE EXCEPTION(3:"
"RenderingAPIException): currentGLContext was specified with no current GL "
"context in GLXWindow::create at ./RenderSystems/GL3Plus/src/windowing/GLX/"
"OgreGLXWindow.cpp (line 165)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:203
msgid "A workaround is to set `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb`. e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:205
msgid "QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb gz sim -v 4 shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:209
msgid ""
"Another workaround to try is to make sure Gazebo is launched with XWayland "
"by unsetting the `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` environment variable, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:212
msgid "env -u WAYLAND_DISPLAY gz sim -v 4 shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:216
msgid "EGL warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:218
msgid "On startup, Gazebo prints out EGL warning messages like the one below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:220
msgid "libEGL warning: DRI2: failed to create dri screen\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:224
msgid ""
"This message is printed out by Ogre 2 on initialization when it enumerates "
"through devices to query for EGL support. The warning is fine to ignore. "
"Gazebo should continue to operate without any issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:228
msgid "Network Configuration Issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:229
msgid ""
"Improper network configuration can cause Gazebo to open a window and then "
"become unresponsive. This issue can be diagnosed by running ```gz sim -v 4 "
"shapes.sdf``` and checking for the following output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:231
msgid ""
"```[GUI] [Dbg] [Gui.cc:343] GUI requesting list of world names. The server "
"may be busy downloading resources. Please be patient.```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:233
msgid ""
"To fix this, enable multicast by following the steps at [ROS Enable "
"Multicast](https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/How-To-Guides/Installation-"
"Troubleshooting.html#enable-multicast)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:236
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:238
msgid ""
"VisualStudioVersion is not set, please run within a Visual Studio Command "
"Prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:239
msgid ""
"When you try to compile Gazebo you might see an error in your prompt like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:241
msgid ""
"VisualStudioVersion is not set, please run within a Visual Studio Command "
"Prompt.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:243
msgid "In this case execute one of the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:244
msgid "CMD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:245
msgid ""
"    \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual "
"Studio\\2019\\Community\\VC\\Auxiliary\\Build\\vcvarsall.bat\" x86_amd64\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:249
msgid "PowerShell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:250
msgid ""
"pushd \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual "
"Studio\\2019\\Community\\Common7\\Tools\"\n"
"cmd /c \"VsDevCmd.bat&set\" |\n"
"foreach {\n"
"  if ($_ -match \"=\") {\n"
"    $v = $_.split(\"=\"); set-item -force -path \"ENV:\\$($v[0])\"  -value "
"\"$($v[1])\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"popd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:261
msgid "Many errors from setuptools when running colcon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:262
msgid ""
"When calling `colcon` to build the packages, you may face a wall of Python "
"errors similar to this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:264
msgid ""
"> colcon graph\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n"
"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'setuptools.extern'\n"
"[10.385s] colcon.colcon_core.package_identification ERROR Exception in "
"package identification extension 'python_setup_py' in 'conda\\Lib\\site-"
"packages\\adodbapi': Command '['D:\\\\programovani\\\\gz-ws\\\\conda\\"
"\\python.exe', '-c', \"import sys;from setuptools.extern.packaging."
"specifiers import SpecifierSet;from distutils.core import run_setup;dist = "
"run_setup(    'setup.py', script_args=('--dry-run',), stop_after='config');"
"skip_keys = ('cmdclass', 'distclass', 'ext_modules', 'metadata');data = "
"{    key: value for key, value in dist.__dict__.items()     if (        not "
"key.startswith('_') and         not callable(value) and         key not in "
"skip_keys and         key not in dist.display_option_names    )};"
"data['metadata'] = {    k: v for k, v in dist.metadata.__dict__.items()     "
"if k not in ('license_files', 'provides_extras')};sys.stdout.buffer."
"write(repr(data).encode('utf-8'))\"]' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:272
msgid ""
"The messages are quite cryptic and do not point at the root cause. The root "
"cause is that you have probably created a conda env directory in the same "
"directory where you have the `src` directory containing the Gazebo sources "
"(you have probably used `conda create --prefix ...` to create the env "
"directory at a non-default destination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:274
msgid "The solution is to move the conda env directory one level up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:276
msgid "E.g., this is the problematic folder structure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:278
msgid ""
"gz-ws\\\n"
"  conda\\  # The conda env\n"
"  src\\    # The Gazebo sources\n"
"    gz-sim\\\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:285
msgid "To fix it, change the structure to something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../troubleshooting.md:287
msgid ""
"gz-ws\\\n"
"  src\\\n"
"    gz-sim\\\n"
"conda\\\n"
msgstr ""
